  "notes": "{開|ひら}く has two main meanings: (1) to open something physical, and (2) to hold/organize an event.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle\n\nDON'T CONFUSE (all use {開|ひら/あ}):\n- {開|ひら}く: to open (formal), to hold events\n- {開|あ}く: to open by itself (intransitive)\n- {開|あ}ける: to open something (transitive, everyday)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {本|ほん}を{開|ひら}く: to open a book\n- {会議|かいぎ}を{開|ひら}く: to hold a meeting\n- パーティーを{開|ひら}く: to throw a party\n- {店|みせ}を{開|ひら}く: to open a shop/business\n- {目|め}を{開|ひら}く: to open one's eyes (literary)\n\nREGISTER:\n{開|ひら}く sounds more formal/literary than {開|あ}ける for physical opening. For events, {開|ひら}く is the standard choice.",
